# Source is source, whatever byte wandered into it.
#
# git decides "binary" by looking for a NUL in the first few kilobytes, and one stray
# control character in a string literal is enough to make a whole file undiffable:
# `Binary files differ`, no lines, nothing to review, and nothing the diff viewer can
# draw. That happened here (a raw NUL in a template literal in renderer/stores/staging.ts,
# commit d85afc6) and the commit is on main for good; the attribute is what makes those
# diffs readable again, retroactively and everywhere, including plain `git diff`.
#
# `diff` only, deliberately: `text` would renormalize line endings across the whole
# repository on the next checkout, which is a much larger change than this is.
*.ts    diff
*.mjs   diff
*.vue   diff
*.css   diff
*.html  diff
*.json  diff
*.md    diff
